# GNU Stow ignore list for this package.
#
# The presence of this file REPLACES stow's built-in default ignore list, so
# everything that must stay unstowed has to be named here explicitly.
#
# Patterns are anchored regexes. One containing "/" matches against the path
# relative to the package root; one without matches the basename at any depth.
# "^/foo" therefore means "foo at the top level only".

# --- VCS and OS noise ---
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules
\.DS_Store

# --- editor backup / autosave files ---
.+~
\#.*\#

# --- run or copied from the checkout, never symlinked into $HOME ---
# Installers, samples, and docs. You invoke or copy these from the repo; a
# symlink in ~ would just be a file nothing reads. Keeping them listed is what
# lets `stow` be run plainly, with no hand-linking of individual files.
^/install\.sh
^/README\.md
^/atlassian-mcp
^/\.zprofile\.sample
^/docs
